Subject: Suppressing unneeded \begin{kframe}..\end{kframe} and how to suppress ##
Message-ID: <G6HSbKxfm50.fDDqLWWwx9gJ@knitr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/knitr/c/G6HSbKxfm50/m/fDDqLWWwx9gJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I am letting the LaTeX listings package do the work of making shaded
boxes and pretty printing R code.  I do this using

\usepackage{listings}
\lstset{language=R}
. . . .
hook_lst_bf = function(x, options) {
  paste('\\begin{lstlisting}[basicstyle={\\bfseries}]\n', x,
        '\\end{lstlisting}\n', sep = '')
}
knit_hooks$set(source = function(x, options) {
  paste('\\begin{lstlisting}[style=Rstyle]\n', x,
        '\\end{lstlisting}\n', sep = '')
},output = function(x, options) {
  paste('\\begin{lstlisting}[style=Routstyle]\n', x,
        '\\end{lstlisting}\n', sep = '')
}, warning = hook_lst_bf, message = hook_lst_bf, error = hook_lst_bf)
set_header(highlight = '')
knit_hooks$set(par=function(before, options, envir) {
 if(before && options$fig.show!='none') spar()}, crop=hook_pdfcrop)
options(replace.assign=TRUE)
% \SweaveOpts{highlight=FALSE, fig.path=figure/graphics-,
fig.align=center, fig.width=4, fig.height=3, fig.show=hold, par=TRUE}

My first question is how do I make knitr supress issuing
\begin{kframe} ... \end{kframe}?  I use the following ugly trick for
now:

\renewenvironment{kframe}{}{}  % let listings do shaded boxes

Secondly, raw R output is prefixed with '##'.  How do I suppress the
## in these R output lines?

Thanks very much,
Frank

