Hi Yihui,

This kind of extensibility is impressive.  I did run into a problem
with dev=my customized function:

knit_hooks$set(plot=function (x, options) {
  if (!options$include)
    return("")
  cap <- options$caption   # FH
...
})

mpdf <- function(file, width, height) {
  g <- function(n, default=NULL, aslist=FALSE) {
    w <- opts_current$get(n)
    w <- if(length(w)) w else default
    if(aslist) structure(list(w), names=n) else w
  }
  pdf(file, width = width, height = height, pointsize = g('pointsize',
12))
  z <- c(g('mfrow', aslist=TRUE), g('bty', 'l', aslist=TRUE),
g('mgp',aslist=TRUE))
  if(length(z)) do.call('spar', z) else spar()
}
opts_knit$set(eval.opts = c('eval', 'echo', 'caption')) # allows
symbolic captions
## see http://yihui.name/knitr/options#package_options
options(replace.assign=TRUE)
@

\SweaveOpts{highlight=FALSE, fig.path=figure/graphics-,
fig.align=center, fig.width=4, fig.height=3, fig.show=hold,
comment=NA, dev=mpdf}
. . .

<<>>=
plot(1:10)
@

Error: device name 'mpdf' not supported yet; please go to
https://github.com/yihui/knitr/issues to report this issue
Execution halted

Thanks for your continued help.
Frank

